  logText: 'April 20th, 2091\n\nCloser scanning of TRAPPIST-1 e confirms previous
    examinations.

    Its total mass is approximately 0.692 Earths.

    It is tidally
    locked. While half the planet constantly receives sunlight, surface temperatures
    don''t seem extreme.

    It takes 146 Earth hours to complete one full orbit
    around its star.

    Its moon is about 15% larger than ours.


    Surface scans
    indicate that the planet likely had substantial amounts of water, with an estimated
    volume of 1 billion cubic kilometres, but it sadly dried out completely. If there
    was ever life here, we are several hundred million years late.


    However,
    some data results seem extremely abnormal. The atmosphere, which is slowly disappearing
    (probably due to the planet''s orbit being extremely close to its star), shows
    a gas composition that simply shouldn''t exist in a barren world like this.


    I
    strongly believe it is worth investigating, which means I need to convince the
    higher-ups to let me go on a solo mission.'
  orderFound: 0
  read: 1
